@host = http://localhost:5235

### Confident match: a known test query, well ahead of the runner-up (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "How do I locate my card?" }

### Ambiguous match: margin between rank 1 and 2 is under 0.02 (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "why did my cash get charged a fee that should not be there." }

### Normalization: different case/whitespace than the stored text still
### reuses its embedding - QueryText.Create collapses both to the same
### normalized text (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "  HOW DO I   locate MY card?  " }

### Request shape: "query" is the only field the endpoint reads. There is
### no top/representation parameter over HTTP - those are CLI-only knobs;
### the endpoint always asks for the top 3 matches by centroid (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "where is the virtual card?" }

### New query: not in the dataset, embedded on the fly (calls OpenAI)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "the barista charged me twice for one iced latte" }

### Off-topic: nothing in Banking77 is close, so every match has low
### similarity (calls OpenAI)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "what's the weather like in Paris this weekend?" }

### 400: empty query (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "" }

### 400: whitespace-only query normalizes to empty (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "   \t  " }

### 400: over QueryText.MaxLength (1000 chars), rejected before any
### embedding call - 1001 "a"s below (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "" }
